+// wwe2k14 patch (Session 66, H1.1 readback_resolve_batch).
+//
+// Why deferring the copy-back is exact: the guest CPU can only act on the output of a resolve after it has seen a
+// completion signal, and the only signals this command processor produces are the points hooked through
+// OnGuestVisibleWrite: a write into guest memory (EVENT_WRITE_SHD fences, EVENT_WRITE_EXT, MEM_WRITE, COND_WRITE,
+// REG_TO_MEM, the occlusion result, scratch register / read pointer write-backs), a guest interrupt callback and a
+// swap. FlushPendingReadbacks runs before each of them, so every queued memcpy has landed in guest memory before the
+// guest could have observed anything newer. Any other wait on the GPU (AwaitAllQueueOperationsCompletion, which is
+// also memexport's and the occlusion readback's) flushes first, so order against the other guest memory writers is
